      "date": "2026-07-27 20:20:27.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 3:\n\n(10 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The mechanical #include_next conversion looks sound, but several hunks are not header normalisation at all - they delete runtime guards in the llite I/O path, change an Xarray error translation, and swap an assertion. Those pieces change client I/O behaviour on every kernel older than v6.4 and would be much easier to review (and to bisect) as their own patches with their own Change-Ids.",
